# P2 Looking For Group Syncronization

This is a synchronization problem.
- Tasked to make LFG dungeon queuing of an MMORPG
- n instances max that can be concurrently active, so there can only be n max number of parties currently in a dungeon
- standard party of 5 is 1 tank, 1 healer, 3 DPS
- solution should not result in deadlocks
- solution should not result in starvation
- it is assumed that input values arrived at the same time
- time value t1 t2, where t1 represents fastest clear time of a dungeon instances and t2 is the slower clear time of a dungeon instance.
- For ease of testing t2 <= 15.

## Input
- n - maximum number of concurrent instances
- t - number of tank players in the queue
- h - number of healers in the queue
- d - number of DPS players in the queue
- t1 - minimum amount of time before an instance is finished
- t2- maximum amount of time before an instance is finished
- any programming language except java or nodejs

## Output
- should updated what parties come in and come out
- if party in instance it should say active
- instance is empty status should say empty
- in the end summary of how many parties an instance served and total time served

## Deliverables
- Source code
- video demo
- source code + build/compilation steps
- slides containing the following:
	- possible deadlock and starvation explanation
	- synchronization mechanisms to solve problem


--------------------------------------------
- compile with make. so learn make basically.